Scope of the Reference Implementation

This reference implementation includes the demo, scripts, and supporting artifacts provided in this repository.

Structural Time (STIME) defines a deterministic structural time model based on valid structural transitions.

The core identity is:

structural_time = count(accepted transitions)

The reference implementation demonstrates:

time emerging from structure (not clocks)
advancement only on valid structural change
duplicate suppression (NO_CHANGE)
invalid transition rejection (ABSTAIN)
deterministic convergence across independent nodes
identical structural time under unordered, unsynchronized execution

This implementation is provided to demonstrate the feasibility of structure-derived time.


Conformance

An implementation is considered compatible with Structural Time (STIME) if it preserves the core structural properties demonstrated by this reference implementation, including:

deterministic transition evaluation
order independence
time independence (no clock dependency)
idempotent behavior under duplicate inputs
explicit handling of invalid transitions (ABSTAIN)
monotonic advancement of structural time
deterministic replay behavior

Conformance is defined by reproducible structural outcomes under permutation, replay, and independent execution.

Independent implementations are permitted and encouraged.


