Closing Statement

Structural Time (STIME) explores the idea that time does not need to be measured externally, but can be derived from deterministic structural transitions.

When structure is consistent, time converges — even without clocks, synchronization, or coordination.

Structural Time is released as an open reference to encourage independent validation, implementation, and exploration of structure-derived temporal systems.

Time is not measured.
Time is resolved.
